From 5563ded6200baee1f191d6b85941091e837c776c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 4 Jul 2026 08:08:45 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?feat(onboarding):=20auto-migrate=20Beads?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=86=92Kernel=20and=20self-install=20hooks=20on=20setup/init?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two onboarding gaps a dogfood test exposed:

Gap 1 — beads→kernel migration was not automatic on install. `forge setup`
(quick/--yes/interactive) and `forge init` now detect a jsonl-backed `.beads`
store and auto-import issues/comments/deps into the Kernel, reusing the
idempotent `forge migrate --from beads` spine. Reads the committed jsonl
sidecars directly — no external issue-tracker CLI required — and surfaces the
same honest field-gap report. New helpers: migrate.detectBeadsJsonlSource /
autoMigrateBeadsIfPresent and setup.autoMigrateBeadsToKernel.

Gap 2 — `forge init` scaffolded `.forge/` but never installed git hooks, so
stage commands hard-stopped on HOOKS_NOT_ACTIVE with no path forward. init now
installs hooks after scaffolding (via setup.ensureGitHooksInstalled, reusing
the same lefthook install setup performs; package.json-gated so bare repos are
untouched). Both steps are idempotent and degrade to a warning, never abort.

Regenerated the D20 bd call-site kill-list (migrate.js additions shifted
command-group counts). setup.js stays bd-free.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
